  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Mix ingredients except sulfur and Na2S·9H2O, adjust pH to 5.5 with H2SO4, and autoclave under H2/CO2 (80/20) conditions. Separately autoclave neutralize Na2S·9H2O solution. Sulfur is sterilized separately by autoclaving for 60 min at 105℃ on each of 3 successive days. Aseptically and anaerobically add sterile sulfur to the medium under a H2/CO2 (80/20) atmosphere. Prior to inoculation, add Na2S·9H2O solution, and readjust pH to 5.5 if necessary. Pressurize inoculated bottles to 200 kPa with H2/CO2 (80/20)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Dissolve nitrilotriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with KOH solution. Then proceed to add minerals. Adjust final pH to 7.0."
    }
  ]
}